# The daily list-check schedule: half an hour after the optimizer's window opens.
#
# The plan says "daily after 03:00" and this is that made concrete. Half an hour
# puts the check after the hour the optimizer starts in, so a check meant to
# report on the day's reference data is not reading it while a measurement run is
# still going. The check holds no lock and only reads the published pair, so if a
# long run is still going at 03:30 the check still works; the one case it does not
# survive is catching a publication in flight, which it reports as an exit 3 rather
# than concluding "up-to-date" from a pair it could not verify.
#
# Persistent, and for the opposite reason the health timer is not: this is a daily
# report. A machine that was off at 03:30 produces the report at next boot, and a
# report nobody will ever be shown is not a report. One catch-up run, once.
#
# To move it, drop in over this timer and reload it -- the commands are the ones in
# mosdns-cdn-optimizer.timer, with this timer's name.

[Unit]
Description=Daily China list drift check schedule

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 03:30:00
Persistent=true
Unit=mosdns-list-check.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target